node_modules/

# sql/schema.sql WAS ignored here, on the theory that `npm run build`'s
# `cp ../supabase/schema.sql` would keep it current and a committed copy would
# only drift. It shipped nothing: hnk-api's App Platform component builds from
# source_dir /server, which does not include the sibling supabase/ directory
# the cp reaches for, so the copy silently never happened in production. The
# gap stayed invisible for as long as platform.sql kept failing first — the
# moment it stopped, /health settled on schema:0 with no error, migrate()
# having found no schema.sql at all. It is now a tracked file for exactly that
# reason, and test/verify_release_contract.js asserts it stays byte-identical
# to supabase/schema.sql instead of a comment asking nicely.
